    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28236" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοχμός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span> (Delph.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			v. infr.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόχμιος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοχμὼ ἀΐσσοντε</span> rushing
			on <i>slantwise,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.148
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοχμοὶ μῆτραι</span>”
				<i>lying obliquely,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					2.141
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀπὸ προβολῆς κλινθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					22.120
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀνακρούων θηρὸς πάτον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					479
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁ ὁδὸς ἁ δοχμά</span> the
				<i>cross</i>-road, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Klio</u>
				16.170
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>). </div>
